    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "After a storm damages your roof, prioritize safety by staying off the roof and inspecting from the ground. Next, document all visible exterior and interior damage with photos and videos, prevent further water leaks using buckets or temporary tarps, contact a licensed local roofer, and file your insurance claim promptly.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "prioritize safety by staying off the roof and inspecting from the ground"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Safety and Protection (First 24 Hours)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check for hazards: Stay away from downed power lines, broken gas lines, and unstable trees or structures."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof: Never climb onto a wet, slippery, or structurally compromised roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect from the ground: Walk around the perimeter to look for missing shingles, dented flashing, or shingle granules in the gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check inside: Look for ceiling leaks, wet insulation, or bulging drywall, and place buckets under active drips."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Stop further water damage: Move furniture and electronics away from leaks, turn off electricity to wet rooms, and hire a pro for emergency roof tarping.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Documentation and Insurance (Day 1 to 3)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Photograph everything: Capture wide-angle shots of the entire property and close-ups of specific roof, siding, and gutter damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Record a video walk-through: Narrate the video with the date, time, and address while panning over damaged areas."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Save all receipts: Keep every invoice for temporary patches, tarps, plywood, or emergency supplies."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Call your insurance company: Open a claim right away, record your claim number, and ask about specific storm or wind deductibles.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Hiring a Contractor and Repair (Days 2 and Beyond)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get a professional inspection: Hire a licensed, insured local roofer to check for hidden damage, such as bruised shingles or compromised decking.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get written estimates: Request a detailed, line-by-line scope of work and price quote.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid door-to-door scammers: Be cautious of \"storm chasers\" who pressure you to sign contracts or offer to waive your insurance deductible.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the insurance adjuster: Walk the property with your insurance adjuster and your roofer so nothing is missed.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of weather caused the damage (hail, high wind, heavy snow, or a fallen tree)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Are you currently seeing active leaks inside your home?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prioritize your next steps or what to tell your insurance company."
      }
    ],
